.TH DEW 1 2026-10-06 "dew 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dew \- terminal to-do list with waves and a Game of Life garden
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dew
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR path ]
.br
.B dew
.RB [ \-\-file
.IR path ]
.B add
.RB [ \-t ]
.I text ...
.br
.B dew
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dew
is a to-do list you knock out with a pomodoro timer.
A pomodoro is called a
.IR wave .
There are two lists:
.B Today
and the
.BR Backlog .
Start a wave on a task, work until the timer ends, take a break, repeat.
.PP
The right-hand pane runs a Game of Life board that reacts to what you do.
Starting a wave seeds it with soft-colored patches, checking off a task
launches a fleet of gliders and sends a wolf running across the board,
finishing a wave sets off a burst and plants a pattern in today's
.IR garden ,
and a break floods the board with a river (a white wolf runs along its bank)
that gives way to Brian's Brain fireworks.
Each task you finish gets the next of five wolves: frost, ember, aurora,
shadow and dusk, at a gallop or a trot.
When several tasks are done at once they run one after another, and the
river waits for a wolf that is still out.
Pausing turns the colony gray and lets it die off.
Garden plants wear Nord gradients that shift as they blink and breathe.
.PP
Focus waves run Conway's Game of Life unless you pick another
simulation: set
.B focus_rule
or press
.BR r .
Breaks always run Brian's Brain and the garden always runs Conway.
The lower right corner of the pane always shows the simulation waves run.
.PP
The pane is hidden when the terminal is smaller than 80\(mu24.
.SH KEYS
.TP 12
.BR j " " k " " \(da " " \(ua
Move the selection. Today and Backlog form one list.
.TP
.BR g " " G
Jump to the top or bottom.
.TP
.B Tab
Jump between Today and Backlog.
.TP
.B a
Add a task to the list the selection is in.
.TP
.B e
Edit the selected task's title.
.TP
.B n
Edit the note in
.BR $VISUAL ,
.BR $EDITOR ,
or
.BR vi .
.TP
.B x
Mark done or not done.
.TP
.B t
Move between Today and Backlog.
.TP
.BR J " " K
Move the task down or up within its list.
.TP
.B d
Delete, after a y/n prompt.
.TP
.B Space
Start a wave on the selected task (or the first open task in Today),
pause it, or resume it. During a break it skips the rest of the break.
.TP
.B s
Finish the wave now (it counts), or end the break.
.TP
.B S
Abandon the wave. It does not count and plants nothing.
.TP
.B m
Switch the wave length: 15, 25 or 45 minutes (plus
.B focus
from the config if it is another).
Breaks are worked out from it; see
.BR WAVES .
During a wave, the wave itself gets the new length and keeps the time
already done; lengths it has already run past are skipped.
The choice is remembered until the config's
.B focus
changes.
.TP
.B r
Switch the simulation that waves run to the next one: conway, highlife,
day & night, seeds, life without death, maze, 2x2, morley, brian's brain,
star wars, then your own rule if the config has one.
The choice is remembered until the config's
.B focus_rule
changes.
.TP
.B w
Show today's garden full screen. Any key returns.
.TP
.B ?
Show the keys.
.TP
.B q
Quit. A running wave is saved and picks up where it was next time.
.PP
In the add and edit prompt:
.B Enter
saves,
.B Esc
cancels,
.B Ctrl\-U
clears to the start, and
.BR \(<- " " \(-> " " Home " " End " " Backspace " " Delete
work as usual.
.SH WAVES
A wave is 25 minutes of focus followed by a 5-minute break, or a
15-minute break after every 4th wave.
Press
.B m
for 15- or 45-minute waves; the breaks keep the config's proportions,
so with the defaults a 15-minute wave has 3- and 9-minute breaks and a
45-minute wave 9- and 27-minute ones (whole minutes, at least one).
The break ends by itself; dew never starts the next wave for you.
At the end of each focus and break dew rings the terminal bell and,
if
.B notify\-send
is installed, shows a desktop notification.
.PP
A finished wave adds one to the task's wave count, shown as
.B \[u16DA]
(laguz, the water rune) followed by the count.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/dew/tasks.md
The tasks (default
.IR ~/.local/share/dew/tasks.md ).
It is plain Markdown and safe to edit by hand, even while dew is
running: dew notices within a second and reloads it.
.RS
.PP
.nf
# Today
\- [ ] fix grub theme <!\-\- dew waves=2 \-\->
  A note is the indented lines under a task.
\- [x] scaffold polymon <!\-\- dew waves=3 done=2026\-10\-02 \-\->

# Backlog
\- [ ] retheme sddm login
.fi
.PP
Lines dew doesn't understand are kept as they are.
Done tasks move to a
.B # Done
.I date
section on the next day.
dew saves after every change through a temporary file, keeps the
previous version as
.IR tasks.md.bak ,
and never overwrites a file it cannot parse; it names the bad line instead.
.RE
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/dew/garden/YYYY\-MM\-DD
One line per finished wave: time, pattern, position, color.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/dew/state
The running wave, so it survives a restart.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dew/config
Settings (default
.IR ~/.config/dew/config ).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dew/colors
Optional overrides for the Nord palette.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file holds
.I key " = " value
lines; # starts a comment.
.TP 14
.BR focus " (25)"
Focus minutes, 1\-180.
The wave length dew starts with;
.B m
switches between this, 15, 25 and 45.
.TP
.BR short_break " (5)"
Break minutes after a
.B focus
length wave, 1\-60; other lengths scale it.
.TP
.BR long_break " (15)"
Long break minutes after a
.B focus
length wave, 1\-120; other lengths scale it.
.TP
.BR long_every " (4)"
A long break after this many waves, 1\-12.
.TP
.BR sprite " (rune)"
.B rune
(\[u16DA]),
.B wave
(\[u1F30A]),
.B ascii
(\(~~) or
.B bolt
(\[u26A1]).
.TP
.BR bell " (1)"
Ring the terminal bell at the end of focus and breaks.
.TP
.BR notify " (1)"
Show desktop notifications.
.TP
.BR fps " (20)"
Animation frames per second, 5\-60.
.TP
.BR glitch " (1)"
0 turns off the glitch tears and rune jitter.
.TP
.BR wolf_graphics " (auto)"
How the wolves are drawn:
.B kitty
(real pixels through kitty's graphics protocol; kitty, ghostty),
.B sixel
(real pixels; foot),
.B braille
(dots, any terminal), or
.B auto
to choose from
.BR TERM ,
.B TERM_PROGRAM
and
.BR KITTY_WINDOW_ID .
Inside tmux, auto uses braille.
.TP
.BR focus_rule " (conway)"
The simulation focus waves run: a preset
.RB ( conway ", " highlife ", " daynight ", " seeds ", " lifewithoutdeath ,
.BR maze ", " 2x2 ", " morley ", " brain ", " starwars )
or a rule string such as
.B B36/S23
or, with dying states,
.BR B2/S345/C4 .
.PP
The colors file takes
.BR nord0 " to " nord15 ,
each as
.IR #rrggbb .
On terminals that allow it (foot, kitty, ghostty) dew shows the exact
colors and restores the terminal's palette when it quits;
elsewhere it uses the nearest of the 256 standard colors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR VISUAL ", " EDITOR
The note editor.
.TP
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where dew keeps its files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when dew cannot start (another dew is running, or
.I tasks.md
has an error), 2 for a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dew add \-t fix the grub theme
Add a task to Today from the shell.
.TP
.B dew \-\-file ~/work/tasks.md
Use a different list.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify\-send (1)
